          "heading": "opening",
          "fact_ids": [
            "age_sex.0",
            "presenting_complaint.0",
            "diagnosis_primary.0"
          ],
          "text": "This 58-year-old female was admitted on 02/04 with necrotising soft-tissue infection of the left thigh and septic shock, representing a 49-day admission discharged on 21/05.",
          "unverified_fact_ids": []
        },
        {
          "section_id": "sections.12",
          "part": "part_b",
          "heading": "admission_summary",
          "fact_ids": [
            "key_investigations.0",
            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5",
            "treatment.6",
            "treatment.7",
            "treatment.8"
          ],
          "text": "Wound and tissue cultures grew Group A Streptococcus and anaerobes. She required full multi-organ support including intubation and ventilation, noradrenaline, and CVVH for AKI. She underwent four surgical debridements (days 0, 2, 5 and 9) with washout, delayed closure and VAC dressing. Antibiotic therapy commenced with IV piperacillin-tazobactam and was subsequently rationalised to benzylpenicillin and clindamycin on microbiology advice. ARDS was managed with two episodes of prone positioning. Lines were changed on day 14 for line sepsis. Nutrition was initially via nasogastric tube, progressing to oral intake. Renal function recovered and CVVH was discontinued on day 16; she was extubated on day 18 and stepped down to the ward on day 24. The remainder of the admission involved prolonged rehabilitation, physiotherapy, and wound healing by secondary intention with district nurse and tissue viability input.",
          "unverified_fact_ids": []
        },
