    "compose_patient": {
      "sections": [
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came into hospital with a serious infection of the soft tissue in your left thigh. This is called a necrotising soft-tissue infection. The infection caused your body to go into septic shock. You also developed:\n- an acute kidney injury\n- a lung condition called ARDS\n- weakness from being in intensive care\n- an infection in one of your lines on day 14\n- a new irregular heart rhythm (atrial fibrillation)"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "Tests on your wound found two types of bacteria: Group A Streptococcus and anaerobes.\n\nTo support your body, you were put on a breathing machine and given medicines to support your blood pressure. You also had kidney support treatment (CVVH).\n\nYou had four operations to clean the infected tissue, on days 0, 2, 5 and 9. After that, the wound was washed out, closed, and a special wound dressing (VAC dressing) was used.\n\nYou were given a long course of antibiotics through a drip. These were later changed to two different antibiotics (benzylpenicillin and clindamycin) on the advice of the microbiology team.\n\nTo help your lungs, you were turned face-down on two occasions.\n\nYour lines were changed on day 14 because of the line infection.\n\nYou were fed through a tube into your stomach at first, then moved on to eating and drinking by mouth.\n\nYour kidneys recovered and the kidney support treatment stopped on day 16. You came off the breathing machine on day 18. You moved to the ward on day 24.\n\nYou had a long period of rehabilitation and physiotherapy. Your wound is healing, with support from the district nurse and tissue viability team."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7",
            "sections.8"
          ],
          "text": "The following follow-up has been arranged:\n- Plastics and wound clinic in 2 weeks\n- Cardiology follow-up for your heart rhythm in 6 weeks\n- ICU follow-up clinic\n- Community physiotherapy and occupational therapy\n\nYour GP will check your kidney function and blood pressure after your kidney injury."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
          "heading": "safety_net",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{SAFETY_NET}}"
        }
